title: Trailer_Story_Board
---
<<HideAllCharacters>>
// 00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<music ambient_gully fadeIn=1>>
//<<sfx bg_gully_loop vol=0.6>>
//<<cut EXT_GULLY_DAY>>
Narrator: In every gully match, there's always one kid who waits.
// 00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
Narrator: Too small to bat. Too slow to field.
Narrator: But sometimes, one of them is different… and only an elder brother can see it.
// 00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:15,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
// Tone note: "Excited" skews upbeat/cartoonish. For a heavy, cinematic beat, prefer restrained urgency.
// Suggest: Determined/Protective urgency — tight jaw, firm eye contact, low but decisive delivery (no shout).
Ramu: Raju! Grab the bat — you're in!
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Surprised>>
// Tone note: Broad "Surprised" can read goofy. Aim for stunned/awed stillness.
// Suggest: Quiet awe — slight inhale, eyes widen subtly, mouth barely parts; keep body still, sound internal.
Raju (monologue): That was the day… I got the chance to prove myself….
//<<music flashback_pad xfade=1.0>>
// 00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<cut FLASHBACK_WARM_TONE>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Neutral>>
Raju (monologue): Bhaiya used to say… there are five things you carry every time you pick up the bat.
// 00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<lowerthird Lesson 1 – Eyes>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: See before you decide. Read the bowler, not the ball.
// 00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<lowerthird Lesson 2 – Feet>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Quiet feet. Quick mind. Settle first.
// 00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<lowerthird Lesson 3 – Hands>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Neutral>>
Ramu: Gentle hands. Let the bat talk.
// 00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<lowerthird Lesson 4 – Timing>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Wait for your moment. Poor or rich — timing's everything.
// 00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<lowerthird Lesson 5 – Temper>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Neutral>>
Ramu: Miss once, breathe. Miss twice… breathe longer.
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Happy>>
// Tone note: "Happy" feels too bright here. The moment should feel grateful and grounded.
// Suggest: Soft gratitude/nostalgia — small, fleeting smile; eyes glassy, voice low and steady.
Raju: I still carry them all, Bhaiya.
// 00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,080
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<music build_light xfade=0.8>>
//<<sfx bat_hit_clean>>
//<<vfx ball_trail_slowmo>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju ExcitedWithBat>>
// Tone note: Big "Excited" reads celebratory. Keep it contained for cinematic weight.
// Suggest: Contained pride/relief — exhale-laugh under breath, micro-smile, shoulders drop slightly; whisper more than cheer.
Raju (smiling): Six runs… I can really play.
// 00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:48,000
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
//<<music STOP fadeOut=0.3>>
//<<sfx cut_silence>>
//<<cut INT_HOUSE_LOWLIGHT>>
<<SetCharacterExpression ShivPrasad Angry>>
// Tone note: Overt "Angry" may feel melodramatic. Heaviness lands better with controlled steel.
// Suggest: Cold stern/weary — flat tone, clipped words, eyes avoidant; no raised volume, weight in pauses.
Father: Cricket? First get ninety percent.
// 00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Worried>>
Raju (monologue): Ninety percent… or no academy.
// 00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,500
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
//<<music bass_pickup tempo=92>>
//<<cut STUDY_TABLE_NIGHT>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Serious>>
Raju: If that's the price… I'll earn it.
// 00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:59,000
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Serious>>
Raju: I'll get ninety… and I'll play.
// 00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<music rise_local tempo=98>>
//<<cut GROUND_LOCAL_DAY>>
<<SetCharacterExpression CoachDev Serious>>
Coach Dev: There's a city tournament next month. Scouts will be watching.
// 00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:08,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
<<SetCharacterExpression CoachDev Neutral>>
Coach Dev: Play well, and I'll be able to fight for waivers and concessions.
// 00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<cut MONTAGE_MORNING_FIELD>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Come on, swing straight, Raju! Don't rush the shot!
// 00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:14,000
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
//<<cut MONTAGE_AFTERNOON_STUDY>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Pinky Angry>>
// Tone note: Full "Angry" could skew comedic with the line. Aim for brisk, tough-love focus.
// Suggest: Firm impatience/caring edge — quick tempo, eyebrow knit, finger tap on page; volume controlled.
Pinky: Focus here, idiot — this question comes every year!
// 00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
<<SetBGSprite PublicSchool>>
//<<cut MONTAGE_EVENING_LIBRARY>>
<<SetCharacterExpression RamCharan Serious>>
RamCharan: Cricket won't feed you, boy. Books will.
// 00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
//<<cut MONTAGE_MOTHER_WORK>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Kamla Worried>>
Kamla: Raju, at least help me wash these plates before you run off!
// 00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,500
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
//<<cut NIGHT_SINGLE_BULB>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Groggy>>
Raju (monologue): Eyes burn… but I can't stop.
// 00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:27,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<cut DAWN_DUSTY_SUNRISE>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Serious>>
Raju (monologue): Every second counts.
// 00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Worried>>
Raju (monologue): I can't drop the ball… not now.
// 00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
<<SetCharacterExpression CoachDev Excited>>
// Tone note: "Excited" reads cheerlead-y. Keep it urgent and grounded.
// Suggest: Low, intense command — compressed breath, narrowed eyes; urgency without pitch lift.
Coach Dev (VO): This is your chance, Raju!
// 00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
<<SetCharacterExpression ShivPrasad Serious>>
Father (VO): Ninety percent, remember.
// 00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Worried>>
Raju (monologue): If I fail either… I lose everything.
// 00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
<<SetBGSprite KohliwadaGround>>
//<<music final_climax peak>>
//<<vfx slowmo_montage>>
<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Serious>>
Raju (monologue): I believed I had talent…
Raju (monologue): But can I prove it — to him?
Raju (monologue): Can I prove it to the world?
// 00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
//<<music fadeOut=2.0>>
//<<cut FADE_TO_BLACK>>
//<<title_card>>
On-screen text: GULLY CHAMP — Chapter 1: The First Innings
On-screen text: Can you prove your talent to the world?
On-screen text: Wishlist on Steam / Coming Soon
===